    "summary": "Closing turn with no further changes: the correction the revised receipt forced has landed, and I spent the remaining budget verifying the record instead of extending it. The sweep checked every receipt any interpretation or knowledge entry cites, every event index against its receipt's event count, and every cited source against the captured materials, and it came back clean — problems: none, seventeen of seventeen receipts cited so no execution is uncited, fourteen questions each carrying an interpretation, twenty-three knowledge entries, sixteen experiments, zero gaps, and no question left without an interpretation. The substance now stands in its corrected form. The main finding is a classification gap in the inbound filter: MsgForgetLeader is the only locally produced message type absent from isLocalMsg, so a peer-form message clears a follower's live leader context and turns the lease that withholds its pre-vote into a grant — measured on both documented inbound paths including the real Node interface, reproduced by a repeat, bounded by the incumbent's own quorum check and by an aftermath receipt showing no committed entry lost, and now shown to need no illegal field at all. The two boundary questions around it are refuted rather than asserted, each with its own reason: the term-less network message needs a sender that leaves a field illegal, and the transfer-campaign chain needs a sender claiming the leader's authority, which the snapshot never asks a receiver to verify — and that second chain is now measured end to end, with the correction that the incumbent's cost is its term and its leadership, not its ballot. I filed no further probe because no remaining turn could interpret its receipt, and I did not declare a stop, since this run carries no finite directed question. Validate: valid=true, no_change=true, no effects, nothing uncited."
